// Esquema de base de datos de Turnia
// Postgres (pensado para Supabase o Neon). El login lo maneja Firebase Auth:
// acá sólo guardamos el perfil (nombre, rol, negocio) enlazado por firebaseUid.

datasource db {
  provider  = "postgresql"
  // Conexión con pooler (PgBouncer, puerto 6543): la usa la app en tiempo de
  // ejecución. directUrl es una conexión directa (puerto 5432) que Prisma
  // necesita para correr migraciones — el pooler en modo "transaction" no
  // soporta el tipo de sesión que las migraciones necesitan.
  url       = env("DATABASE_URL")
  directUrl = env("DIRECT_URL")
}

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

enum Role {
  CLIENTE
  NEGOCIO
  ADMIN
}

enum EstadoTurno {
  PENDIENTE
  CONFIRMADO
  CANCELADO
  COMPLETADO
}

model User {
  id          String   @id @default(cuid())
  firebaseUid String   @unique
  name        String
  lastName    String?
  email       String   @unique
  phone       String?
  role        Role     @default(CLIENTE)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())

  business     Business?     @relation("BusinessOwner")
  appointments Appointment[] @relation("ClientAppointments")
}

model Business {
  id          String   @id @default(cuid())
  slug        String   @unique
  name        String
  category    String
  description String?
  address     String?
  phone       String?
  whatsapp    String?
  coverImage  String?
  published   Boolean  @default(true)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())

  ownerId String @unique
  owner   User   @relation("BusinessOwner", fields: [ownerId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  services      Service[]
  professionals Professional[]
  hours         BusinessHour[]
  appointments  Appointment[]

  @@index([category])
}

model BusinessHour {
  id         String  @id @default(cuid())
  businessId String
  business   Business @relation(fields: [businessId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  dayOfWeek  Int // 0 = domingo ... 6 = sábado
  isClosed   Boolean @default(false)
  openTime   String? // "10:00"
  closeTime  String? // "20:00"

  @@unique([businessId, dayOfWeek])
}

model Professional {
  id         String  @id @default(cuid())
  businessId String
  business   Business @relation(fields: [businessId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  name       String
  photo      String?
  active     Boolean @default(true)

  appointments Appointment[]
}

model Service {
  id          String  @id @default(cuid())
  businessId  String
  business    Business @relation(fields: [businessId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  category    String
  name        String
  description String?
  price       Float
  durationMin Int     @default(30)
  active      Boolean @default(true)

  appointments Appointment[]

  @@index([businessId])
}

model Appointment {
  id             String      @id @default(cuid())
  businessId     String
  business       Business    @relation(fields: [businessId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  professionalId String
  professional   Professional @relation(fields: [professionalId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  serviceId      String
  service        Service     @relation(fields: [serviceId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  clientId       String
  client         User        @relation("ClientAppointments", fields: [clientId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  startsAt     DateTime
  endsAt       DateTime
  status       EstadoTurno @default(CONFIRMADO)
  notes        String?
  reminderSent Boolean     @default(false)
  createdAt    DateTime    @default(now())

  @@index([businessId, startsAt])
  @@index([professionalId, startsAt])
  @@index([clientId])
}
